RiWork's Simulator adapter is an original Objective-C implementation using
private Apple framework interfaces. Its interface investigation was informed by:

SimKit, https://github.com/subdiox/SimKit (Apache License 2.0), including its
acknowledgement of tddworks/baguette. In particular, the native framebuffer
callback API and the IOHID digitizer wrapper's routing/edge offsets were checked
against SimKit's published implementation.

Meta idb, https://github.com/facebook/idb (MIT License), copyright Meta Platforms,
Inc. and affiliates. Its Simulator API documentation and Indigo constants were
used to verify the persistent HID client's selectors and Home button target.

These projects are not dependencies of the built helper. Apple private
frameworks are loaded from the user's selected Xcode installation.
